This file declares tests/fixtures/ as a TEST-CONTROLLED PROVIDER FIXTURE ROOT for the MAF Scoring
Runner v2.

evaluation/experiments/scoring/lib/provider-identity.ts refuses to approve a test-double provider
executable unless it lives inside a directory tree carrying this marker file. A test's own temporary
fixture directory writes one; the operator's real Claude Code installation directory never will.

That is the second half of test-double identification. The first half is the
MAF_SCORING_TEST_DOUBLE_PROVIDER_V2 token inside the executable's own bytes, which proves WHAT the
file is; this file proves WHERE it is allowed to come from. Both must hold, because either alone is
weaker than it looks: a marker with no root would approve a marked script an attacker or a careless
refactor dropped anywhere on disk, and a root with no marker would approve the real Claude binary if
someone ever copied it in here.

Do not add this file to a directory that contains, or could come to contain, a real provider
executable.

